        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis is a [documented behavior](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/3923662bf3d6ca49a9503f8d7196ea0450983e6a/doc/mini-ai.txt#L567-L577). The default `an` / `in` mappings existed way before the new built-in ones and changing them would be breaking. And 'mini.ai' ones are useful in their own right.\n\nThe linked documentation abouve describes the suggested workaround for LSP based incremental selection. Unfortunately, there is no public method for tree-sitter based incremental selection (see neovim/neovim#38211), so there won't be a good solution for that. I waited for 0.12 release to find the best approach and update the docs, but I am still not sure about how to approach this best.\n\nAll in all, this is an expected behavior.",
